## 🎯 Key Principles

1. **Single Responsibility**: Each layer has one clear purpose
2. **Dependency Direction**: Always call down the hierarchy, never up
3. **Locator Isolation**: ONLY AIElement accesses locators
4. **No Skipping**: Each layer calls only the layer directly below
5. **Business Independence**: Business classes don't call each other

---

## ✅ Architecture Compliance Checklist

- [ ] Test Scenarios ONLY call Business layer methods
- [ ] Test Scenarios contain NO direct locators
- [ ] Test Scenarios have NO direct Playwright page interactions
- [ ] Business Workflows ONLY call Page Object methods
- [ ] Business Workflows contain NO direct locators
- [ ] Business Workflows have NO direct page interactions
- [ ] Business Workflows have NO cross-business calls
- [ ] Page Objects use AIElement for ALL interactions
- [ ] Page Objects contain NO direct locators
- [ ] Page Objects have NO direct `this.page` calls
- [ ] AIElement is ONLY class accessing locators from cache
- [ ] Proper call hierarchy maintained at all times

---

## 🎯 Success Criteria

- ✅ **Proper Layering**: Test → Business → Page Objects → AIElement → Cache
- ✅ **No Direct Locators**: Zero locators in high-level code
- ✅ **No Direct Page Access**: Zero `this.page` calls in high-level code
- ✅ **Single Responsibility**: Each layer focuses on its purpose
- ✅ **Maintainability**: Clear separation of concerns
- ✅ **Testability**: Each layer can be tested independently
